Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.210 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Stephanie bissonnette who played high  school student Don Schweitzer in Mean  Girls the musical has died she was 32  years old  [Music]  the Broadway production announced the  sad news on Twitter writing that their  hearts are broken quote she filled our  theater with her laughter and friendship  inspired us with her fighting spirit and  bravery and gray star stage with the  fiercest Talent Broadway has ever known  [Music]  all right  the statement went on adding that you  will be missed profoundly before  encouraging everyone to do something  they love today in Stephanie's honor  Stephanie was a part of the Broadway  company from the first performance in  2018 to the last in 2020 and while a  cause of death has yet to be revealed  according to playbill Stephanie was  previously diagnosed with a rare form of  brain cancer in 2019 but after  undergoing treatment she was able to  return to the show and resume performing  [Music]  following the news of her death fellow  mean girls the musical Alum Ashley Park  posted a lengthy heartfelt tribute to  Instagram writing that her friend's life  was nothing short of a Triumph and  watching Stephanie fight to the end has  been one of the greatest honors of her  life it's worth noting Ashley is a  cancer survivor and recently opened up  about her journey on today with Hoda and  Jenna I was 15 you want to not have  anything to find you that's right and I  really didn't want to have I wanted to  one day be on a talk show and have long  hair and nobody would have any idea I  had cancer you know but I think that  attitude has really informed the person  that I am today in that same interview  Ashley gave a shout out to Stephanie  just days before her death my friend  Stephanie she's battling and fighting  for her life right now and she performed  with me and Mean Girls so please  in addition to her role in Mean Girls  the musical Stephanie helped choreograph  for the muni Riverside Theater  Shakespeare Theater Company and seven  Angel Cedar she also appeared in music  videos including Keith Urban's never  coming down  coming back

